(2872751, 397269, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals: Centered composition and horizon line works in shots with symmetry.  I think it works here.  The light source is blown, but that is to be expected.  The processing is likely where this image failed from the technicals.  The keychain portion has become very choppy with significant portions lost in the dark background.  It has also become quite pixelated which is a limitation of the 640 pixel canvas.<br/> <br/>The feel:  Meets the challenge.  The title is a bit long. I do like the glow of the car.  The keychain, less so.<br/> <br/>The game: Shots of trinkets rarely do well on DPC.  You have to either really nail them technically or have something very unusual.  This likely hurt you a bit in scoring.</td>', 'The technicals: Centered composition and horizon line works in shots with symmetry.  I think it works here.  The light source is blown, but that is to be expected.  The processing is likely where this image failed from the technicals.  The keychain portion has become very choppy with significant portions lost in the dark background.  It has also become quite pixelated which is a limitation of the 640 pixel canvas. The feel:  Meets the challenge.  The title is a bit long. I do like the glow of the car.  The keychain, less so. The game: Shots of trinkets rarely do well on DPC.  You have to either really nail them technically or have something very unusual.  This likely hurt you a bit in scoring.', '2006-09-28 13:31:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2872882, 398397, 64446, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone for voting, specially those who took the time to comment on my very first DPC. They are of great value for me.<br/> <br/>I tried to get away from the common ground like the power lines or messy cables, etc (those came first to my mind - and to others too), and do something different and subtle.<br/>This pic was taken on the very last day of the contest and didn''t have much time to elaborate or do a better PP.<br/> <br/>Again, thanks a lot!</td>', 'Thank you everyone for voting, specially those who took the time to comment on my very first DPC. They are of great value for me. I tried to get away from the common ground like the power lines or messy cables, etc (those came first to my mind - and to others too), and do something different and subtle.This pic was taken on the very last day of the contest and didn''t have much time to elaborate or do a better PP. Again, thanks a lot!', '2006-09-28 14:22:05.000000', NULL, 0),
