(2873685, 398291, 57886, '<td valign="top">Good one... Congrats on your personal best and your new equipment :o)</td>', 'Good one... Congrats on your personal best and your new equipment :o)', '2006-09-28 19:32:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2874312, 398209, 45475, '<td valign="top">Hey hey... not a bad finish considering you were worried about DNMCs. I thought it a great take on the challenge and wondered how it would go. Gave it a 10 without batting an eyelid. The noise didn''t particularly bother me. You captured a perfect James Morrison moment (or any great brass muso for that matter)- the screwed up face, sweaty brow and forehead thanks to lights and of course, effort.<br/> <br/>Fantastic work! :)<br/>Cheers<br/>Rina.</td>', 'Hey hey... not a bad finish considering you were worried about DNMCs. I thought it a great take on the challenge and wondered how it would go. Gave it a 10 without batting an eyelid. The noise didn''t particularly bother me. You captured a perfect James Morrison moment (or any great brass muso for that matter)- the screwed up face, sweaty brow and forehead thanks to lights and of course, effort. Fantastic work! :)CheersRina.', '2006-09-28 23:28:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2874914, 398300, 60165, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Art Roflmao:</b></div><hr/><i> Hmmmm, one entry, no comments made or received no other participation on the site and a very impossible-in-basic looking image. I''ll reserve congratulations until after verification. If all goes well, I shall eat crow. Until then - Hmmmmm... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is a fairly new bridge in Copenhagen, and although I have not seen it myself (yet), I believe it has a unique lighting system. I think it is a pedestrian-bicycle bridge, and tried to find other pictures of it on the internet, but failed :-)<br/> <br/>Has it been validated yet?</td>', 'Originally posted by Art Roflmao: Hmmmm, one entry, no comments made or received no other participation on the site and a very impossible-in-basic looking image. I''ll reserve congratulations until after verification. If all goes well, I shall eat crow. Until then - Hmmmmm...   This is a fairly new bridge in Copenhagen, and although I have not seen it myself (yet), I believe it has a unique lighting system. I think it is a pedestrian-bicycle bridge, and tried to find other pictures of it on the internet, but failed :-) Has it been validated yet?', '2006-09-29 05:36:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2875058, 398300, 53572, '<td valign="top">i found a few images of the bridge on the internet - from plans from the construction to an obviously acmera ''phone image on flickr.  this is an amazing shot of an amazing bridge.  well done.  <br/> <br/>the bridge is called bryggebroen, and it is a moveable bridge over the harbour - the cetral section pivots on an axis to allow large boats through.<br/> <br/>cool.</td>', 'i found a few images of the bridge on the internet - from plans from the construction to an obviously acmera ''phone image on flickr.  this is an amazing shot of an amazing bridge.  well done.   the bridge is called bryggebroen, and it is a moveable bridge over the harbour - the cetral section pivots on an axis to allow large boats through. cool.', '2006-09-29 08:11:36.000000', NULL, 0),
